{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"1c0366f924b5f0c3f0d0ba12b0e9b2093130b58ac1f781d9101f7617c8454b1c","occurred_at":"2026-11-27T23:08:25Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_verified":true,"failure_class":"evidence","mapped_intervals":[[980,981]],"mapped_path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py","quoted_text":"    seeded = seed_drain_work(kind)\n    unrelated, unrelated_state = spawn_detached(\"crq-drain-unrelated\")","reason":"The code acquires `seeded` and `unrelated` before entering the `try`/`finally`; `cleanup` is initialized only after `spawn_detached`. If `spawn_detached` raises after `seed_drain_work` succeeds, the cleanup scope is never entered and the seeded child/run metadata can remain. This is an implementation cleanup defect in the fixture harness, not a new requirement.","target":"4d3b14654a71198e0310c650a203ca91210f8104"},"finding_id":"981bd829c82aeb8dd308c33d81aa583cb99a9379f6cacff2fd851808a1f93296","previous_event_id":"732e42c595bdddc4476dffc4020608056917d8a7e6a57817c44d4ed04a544ad7","review_id":"601e5ffadd611fcbbec00c12d6fa15faccb311c1cf04c2f9b88a9dae9141dc08"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:981bd829c82aeb8dd308c33d81aa583cb99a9379f6cacff2fd851808a1f93296:88df0093c3555fc77c94fcdf02a6635a2463c5fddbe1553b8379c1abb2eb677f"}